WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.480
the newspaper chase. The time is one o'clock in the morning.

00:09.640 --> 00:30.310
The place is the rights-filled town art gallery. A window opens and a man comes in. His name is Harry Black, and he is a thief. It is dark in the art gallery, but Harry has a

00:30.360 --> 00:36.980
light. He looks across the room at a painting. There it is,

00:37.740 --> 00:45.320
he says. Harry moves quickly across the room. He stands and looks at the painting.

00:46.200 --> 01:02.730
A million dollars for this, he thinks. I don't understand it, but he takes a knife from his coat. Then he takes the painting very, very slowly from its

01:02.780 --> 01:20.790
frame. Harry goes back across the room to the window, but he walks into a table. There is a beautiful blue glass vase on the table. It falls on the floor and breaks into a hundred

01:20.840 --> 01:43.530
pieces. Harry smiles. Is that a million dollar vase, he thinks. It isn't now. He runs across the pieces of glass to the window. Harry has a room in Mrs. Allen's

01:43.580 --> 02:04.070
room, quietly up to his room and closes the door. Mrs. Allen and her daughter, Janie, are sleeping. They don't hear him. In his room, Harry takes the painting from his bag. He puts it in a newspaper. Then he puts the

02:04.120 --> 02:14.280
newspaper under his bed. In the morning, Janie Allen is in the kitchen. She's putting old bottles into a box.

02:15.720 --> 02:31.210
Recycling is important, Janie thinks. On the TV, a reporter is at the rightsville art gallery. He is talking about the painting. It's a million dollar

02:31.260 --> 02:49.570
painting, he is saying. Here's a photo of it. Now the reporter is talking about the blue glass vase. It's in a hundred pieces now, he says. Janie looks at the photo of

02:49.620 --> 03:00.140
the vase. Then she asks her mother. Do you have any old bottles? No, Mrs. Allen says.

03:01.140 --> 03:06.220
That's all, Janie. But the newspaper recycling truck is coming today.

03:07.580 --> 03:27.000
Of course, Janie says. It's Friday. Harry isn't in his room. He is talking on his telephone to a man in Seattle. The man wants the painting, but Harry isn't happy.

03:28.000 --> 03:41.380
$5,000, Harry says. No, it's a million dollar painting. What? No,

03:42.320 --> 03:59.940
I want 50,000, not five. What? The painting. Yes, I have it. And it's okay. Janie is looking for old

03:59.990 --> 04:06.830
newspapers. Early on Friday mornings, she takes them from every room in the house.

04:07.830 --> 04:27.680
Then, later, the newspaper recycling truck arrives. Janie opens Harry's door and looks into his room. She always takes his old newspapers or bottles for recycling. Ah, she thinks. There's

04:27.730 --> 04:35.890
a newspaper under Harry's bed. Janie puts the old newspapers into a black recycling box.

04:36.770 --> 04:43.270
She runs from the house and sees the truck. Wait, she says,

04:43.830 --> 04:54.720
and she quickly gives the box to one of the men. Harry is coming back to the house. He sees the recycling truck,

04:54.770 --> 05:04.750
and he sees Janie. It's Friday, he says. The newspaper. Oh, no.

05:06.690 --> 05:08.890
Harry chases after the truck.

05:09.870 --> 05:31.420
Wait, wait. He says. Janie watches him. What is he doing? She thinks. Harry jumps into the back of the truck. I want my newspaper, he says. Where's my

05:31.470 --> 05:41.870
newspaper? But there are thousands of newspapers in the truck. Janie walks quickly from the house to the truck.

05:42.810 --> 05:50.430
Why is your newspaper important, Harry? She asks. It's two days old,

05:50.950 --> 05:53.510
but Harry doesn't hear her.

05:54.290 --> 06:02.760
He is thinking, my million dollar painting. Where is it? The men from the recycling truck

06:02.810 --> 06:08.490
are watching Harry too. But now Janie is looking at Harry's shoe.

06:10.050 --> 06:30.620
There's some blue glass and Harry's shoe, Janie thinks. Where? Oh. Suddenly, she remembers the photo of the blue glass face on the TV. She looks again at the piece of glass and Harry's

06:30.670 --> 06:42.100
shoe. Is it from the vase in the art

06:42.150 --> 06:47.470
of the recycling truck are angry? We're going now. They are saying.

06:48.170 --> 06:57.680
We're late. But I want my newspaper, Harry says. In the house, Janie is talking to the police

06:57.730 --> 07:01.280
on the telephone. Maybe I'm wrong,

07:01.330 --> 07:09.130
she is saying. But there's blue glass in his shoe. What? Yes,

07:09.550 --> 07:11.850
he's looking for the newspaper now.

07:13.810 --> 07:23.490
Two policemen arrive quickly. Let's look at your shoe. They say to Harry. Harry doesn't understand.

07:24.450 --> 07:31.150
What's wrong? He asks. One of the policemen takes the glass from Harry's shoe.

07:32.450 --> 07:40.190
This is a very expensive piece of glass, he says, from a very expensive vase. Remember?

07:41.930 --> 07:52.410
Suddenly, Harry understands. Oh, no, he says. Police cars and policemen arrive.

07:53.490 --> 07:58.830
The men look in the truck for the million dollar painting. Later,

07:59.330 --> 08:01.190
they find the right newspaper

08:01.950 --> 08:07.660
and they find the painting. Good work, Janie, one of the policemen

08:07.710 --> 08:11.010
says. And there's a reward.

08:12.410 --> 08:19.570
Maybe I can buy a painting with a reward, Janie says. I like pictures.
